# Line endings.
#
# This repository stores text as LF and checks it out as LF on every platform. Declaring
# it here rather than leaving it to each clone's core.autocrlf is what makes it hold for
# every tool that writes a file: git normalizes on commit, so an editor or a script that
# writes CRLF -- Python's open() and pathlib.write_text() do exactly that on Windows,
# translating "\n" to os.linesep -- cannot turn a two-line change into a whole-file diff.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the exception. A batch file is safest with CRLF in the working tree, so
# these are stored as LF like everything else and only checked out differently.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Vendored third-party SDK headers, kept byte-for-byte as they were shipped. They carry
# their own copyright notices and are not ours to reformat, and leaving them alone means
# re-vendoring a header from the vendor's own archive does not land as a whole-file diff.
# Only the headers are exempt: the Python beside them in these directories is ours.
acq4/util/clibrary/headers/*.h -text
acq4/drivers/QImaging/*.h -text
acq4/drivers/pvcam/*.h -text

# Binaries, declared rather than left to content detection.
*.png binary
*.npy binary
*.dat binary
